The patch corrects the vulnerability by ensuring that bounds validation occurs unconditionally before any memory operations, regardless of which display update path is taken.

**Change 1: Unconditional Bounds Validation**
<enforcement spec="HS-MEM-003">
<location>hw/cirrus_vga.c, cirrus_bitblt_videotovideo_copy()</location>
<diff>
 static int cirrus_bitblt_videotovideo_copy(CirrusVGAState * s)
 {
-    if (s->ds->dpy_copy) {
+    if (BLTUNSAFE(s))
+        return 0;
+
+    if (s->ds->dpy_copy) {
        cirrus_do_copy(s, s->cirrus_blt_dstaddr - s->start_addr,
                       s->cirrus_blt_srcaddr - s->start_addr,
                       s->cirrus_blt_width, s->cirrus_blt_height);
    } else {
-        if (BLTUNSAFE(s))
-            return 0;

        (*s->cirrus_rop) (s, s->vram_ptr +
                (s->cirrus_blt_dstaddr & s->cirrus_addr_mask),
                          s->vram_ptr +
                (s->cirrus_blt_srcaddr & s->cirrus_addr_mask),
                          s->cirrus_blt_dstpitch, s->cirrus_blt_srcpitch,
                          s->cirrus_blt_width, s->cirrus_blt_height);

        cirrus_invalidate_region(s, s->cirrus_blt_dstaddr,
                                 s->cirrus_blt_dstpitch, s->cirrus_blt_width,
                                 s->cirrus_blt_height);
    }

    return 1;
 }
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix moves the `BLTUNSAFE(s)` bounds check outside and before the `if (s->ds->dpy_copy)` conditional block. This ensures that validation of the guest-supplied BitBLT parameters against the VRAM buffer bounds is performed unconditionally, as the first step in the function. If the parameters are unsafe, the function returns 0 immediately, preventing any memory operations in either code path. This restores compliance with HS-MEM-003 by guaranteeing bounds validation precedes access.
    </compliance_mechanism>
</enforcement>

