	  string->space = more_space;
	}
    }
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix introduces proactive overflow checking before performing the multiplication. It calculates `max_space` as the maximum safe allocation considering both integer limits (`G_MAXINT`) and platform memory constraints (`G_MAXSIZE` divided by element size). The growth calculation uses unsigned integers to avoid signed overflow semantics and checks if doubling would exceed `max_space` before assigning the new value.
    </compliance_mechanism>
</enforcement>

