The patch corrects the packet size validation logic to properly enforce hardware constraints based on the LPE (Long Packet Enable) flag configuration.

**Change 1: Corrected Size Validation Logic**
<enforcement spec="HS-INPUT-001">
<location>hw/e1000.c, e1000_receive()</location>
<diff>
    /* Discard oversized packets if !LPE and !SBP. */
-   if (size > MAXIMUM_ETHERNET_VLAN_SIZE
-       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_LPE)
-       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_SBP)) {
-       return size;
-   }
+   if ((size > MAXIMUM_ETHERNET_LPE_SIZE ||
+       (size > MAXIMUM_ETHERNET_VLAN_SIZE
+       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_LPE)))
+       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_SBP)) {
+       return size;
+   }
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix restructures the conditional logic to properly enforce hardware constraints:
        1. First, it checks if the packet exceeds the absolute maximum size (16384 bytes) regardless of LPE setting. Any packet > 16384 bytes should be discarded when SBP is disabled.
        2. Second, it adds the proper LPE-dependent check: if LPE is disabled AND the packet exceeds VLAN max size (1522 bytes), it should be discarded when SBP is disabled.
        3. Both conditions are combined with OR logic, ensuring that if EITHER condition is true, the packet is rejected when SBP is disabled.
        This correctly implements the hardware specification: when LPE=0, packets > 1522 bytes are rejected; when LPE=1, packets > 16384 bytes are rejected (both subject to SBP override).
    </compliance_mechanism>
</enforcement>

<enforcement spec="HS-PROTOCOL-002">
<location>hw/e1000.c, e1000_receive()</location>
<diff>
    /* Discard oversized packets if !LPE and !SBP. */
-   if (size > MAXIMUM_ETHERNET_VLAN_SIZE
-       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_LPE)
-       && !(s->mac_reg[RCTL] & E1000_RCTL_SBP)) {
-       return size;
-   }
