</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix ensures that Ethernet frame processing respects the MTU boundaries defined by hardware capabilities. By properly checking both the absolute maximum (16384 bytes) and the LPE-dependent maximum (1522 bytes when LPE=0), the emulator now correctly enforces the protocol boundaries as specified by the Intel e1000 hardware. The SBP flag is properly respected as an override mechanism for both conditions.
