 	return 0;
 }
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix modifies `aio_setup_single_vector()` to:
        1. Accept the operation type (`READ`/`WRITE`) and file pointer as parameters
        2. Call `rw_verify_area()` to perform comprehensive boundary validation
        3. Use the validated byte count returned by `rw_verify_area()` instead of the untrusted `ki_left`

        This ensures that integer overflow checks (`ki_pos + ki_left`), mandatory locking verification, and security module checks are performed before any I/O operation proceeds.
    </compliance_mechanism>
</enforcement>

