**Supporting Function: m_strcasestr Implementation**
The fix relies on the `m_strcasestr()` function which provides case-insensitive substring matching:
```c
char *m_strcasestr(const char *haystack, const char *needle) {
    char aux, lower_aux;
    int length;

    if ((aux = *needle++) != 0) {
        aux = (char)tolower((unsigned char)aux);
        length = strlen(needle);
        do {
            do {
                if ((lower_aux = *haystack++) == 0)
                    return NULL;
            } while ((char)tolower((unsigned char)lower_aux) != aux);
        } while (strncasecmp(haystack, needle, length) != 0);
        haystack--;
    }
    return ((char *)haystack);
}
```
This function converts both the search character and the haystack character to lowercase before comparison, ensuring case-insensitive matching throughout the search process.

