        The fix removes the `efree(mfn);` statement. This enforces correct memory ownership semantics by ensuring that `efree` is only called with pointers that are known to be owned by the heap allocator. The stack variable `mfn` is never allocated on the heap, so it must never be freed. This change validates the deallocation operation by restricting it to valid heap pointers only.
