    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix inserts a validation check immediately before accessing the endpoint descriptor. It reads the `bNumEndpoints` field from the interface descriptor and verifies it is at least 1. If the check fails, the probe function aborts with an error (`-EINVAL`) and jumps to the `fail3` cleanup label. This ensures the endpoint descriptor is only accessed after confirming its existence, fully complying with HS-INPUT-001.
    </compliance_mechanism>
