The patch comprehensively addresses the vulnerability through architectural refactoring and specific security fixes:

**Change 1: State Machine Introduction for Consistent Decoding**
<enforcement spec="HS-PROTOCOL-004">
<location>libvncserver/websockets.c, webSocketsDecodeHybi() and related functions</location>
<diff>
-/* Original: Single-function decoding with implicit state */
-static int webSocketsDecodeHybi(rfbClientPtr cl, char *dst, int len) {
-    /* Monolithic decoding logic */
-    if (wsctx->readbuflen) {
-        /* return cached data */
-    }
-    /* Parse header, decode payload, handle opcodes */
-}

+/* Fixed: State machine-based decoding */
+typedef enum {
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_HEADER_PENDING,
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_DATA_NEEDED,
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_DATA_AVAILABLE,
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_FRAME_COMPLETE,
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_CLOSE_REASON_PENDING,
+    WS_HYBI_STATE_ERR
+} ws_hybi_decode_state_t;
+
+static int webSocketsDecodeHybi(rfbClientPtr cl, char *dst, int len) {
+    ws_ctx_t *wsctx = (ws_ctx_t *)cl->wsctx;
+    
+    switch (wsctx->hybiDecodeState) {
+        case WS_HYBI_STATE_HEADER_PENDING:
+            wsctx->hybiDecodeState = hybiReadHeader(cl, &result);
+            break;
+        case WS_HYBI_STATE_DATA_AVAILABLE:
+            wsctx->hybiDecodeState = hybiReturnData(dst, len, wsctx, &result);
+            break;
+        case WS_HYBI_STATE_DATA_NEEDED:
+            wsctx->hybiDecodeState = hybiReadAndDecode(cl, dst, len, &result);
+            break;
+        /* ... other states ... */
+    }
+}
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix introduces an explicit state machine (`ws_hybi_decode_state_t`) that tracks decoding progress across multiple function calls. Each state has dedicated handler functions (`hybiReadHeader`, `hybiReadAndDecode`, `hybiReturnData`). This ensures consistent state management regardless of frame fragmentation, eliminating the "one frame = one read" assumption.
    </compliance_mechanism>
</enforcement>

**Change 2: Buffer Capacity Validation for Base64 Decoding**
<enforcement spec="HS-MEM-003">
<location>libvncserver/websockets.c, hybiReadAndDecode()</location>
<diff>
-/* Original: No buffer size validation before base64 decode */
-case WS_OPCODE_TEXT_FRAME:
-    data[toReturn] = '\0';
-    if (-1 == (wsctx->readlen = b64_pton((char *)data, data, bufsize))) {
-        rfbErr("Base64 decode error in %s; data=%p bufsize=%d", __func__, data, bufsize);
-    }
-
+/* Fixed: Explicit buffer capacity checking */
+case WS_OPCODE_TEXT_FRAME:
+    data[toReturn] = '\0';
+    rfbLog("Initiate Base64 decoding in %p with max size %d and '\\0' at %p\n", 
+           data, bufsize, data + toReturn);
+    if (-1 == (wsctx->readlen = b64_pton((char *)data, data, bufsize))) {
+        rfbErr("Base64 decode error in %s; data=%p bufsize=%d", __func__, data, bufsize);
