    <compliance_mechanism>
        The fix inserts a new validation check using `looks_like_command_line_option(value)` before processing the URL. This function returns true if the string starts with a dash character. When such a URL is detected, the code calls `warn_command_line_option()` to issue a warning and skips storing the malicious URL. This ensures that external configuration data is validated for command-line option syntax before being processed and stored.
