**Change 2: Implement Command-Line Option Detection Function**
<enforcement spec="HS-CONF-002">
<location>parse-options.c (or similar utility file), looks_like_command_line_option()</location>
<diff>
+int looks_like_command_line_option(const char *str)
+{
+	return str && str[0] == '-';
+}
</diff>
    <compliance_mechanism>
        This new utility function implements a syntactic whitelist check: it rejects any string that starts with a dash character. This is a minimal but effective pattern validation that prevents the most common form of command-line option injection. The function provides a reusable validation primitive that can be used throughout the codebase to enforce safe patterns for values that will become command-line arguments.
    </compliance_mechanism>
